  "slug": "variant-regulatory-8ba2",
  "summary": "New preprints dissect what transcriptomic foundation model features encode and test frozen embeddings for imputation, translation and cytokine-response tasks.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is examining and reusing learned representations of gene expression rather than reporting accuracy alone. Sparse autoencoders applied to transcriptomic foundation models yield concept-labeled features that largely behave as gene detectors on spatial panels. A separate test shows a 4-D value track and simple encodings retain most performance in single-cell foundation models, questioning 512-dimensional value embeddings for gene counts. Frozen embeddings are also being repurposed: CYTAP adapts them with baseline-relative representations to infer responses across 90 cytokines, and SimpleP2G finds Virchow2 image features with a simple frozen-embedding decoder effective for predicting expression from pathology images. A second strand handles cross-context inference: BRIDGE uses contrastive learning to impute donor-specific expression across GTEx tissues, and scXOrGAN translates single-cell transcriptomes between organs from cell-unpaired data. GASTON-VI learns spatial axes and molecular gradients from multi-sample spatial omics, and AUTOENCODIX provides a model hub benchmarked on 3.7 million human cells.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-28"
}
